  "transcription_notes": "Gunda Gunde GG-00106, 1 Kings. Single scribal book hand, three columns per page, brown/black ink with red rubrication for section dividers and an occasional small-script red interpretive gloss (an 'እትርጓቱ'-type marginal/interlinear layer that paraphrases the surrounding episode; e.g. on f029r before the chapter, and on f029v-mid summarising the Joab-at-the-altar scene). Those small red gloss runs are a SEPARATE editorial layer, not running scripture, and are NOT carried into the verse text; they are recorded here only as a feature note. The running scripture is the black-ink text and the inline ✣ red crosses (transcribed verbatim as section/clause dividers). CHAPTER START: f029r middle column. 1 Kings 1 fills f029r left column + the top ~16 lines of the middle column and ends with Solomon's words to Adonijah ('...ወይቤሎ ሰሉሞን እቱ ... ቤከ'); 1 Kings 2 v.1 begins immediately after at 'ወሶበ በጽሐ መዋዕሊሁ ለዳዊት ለመዊት እዘዘ ለሰሉሞን' (the days of David drew near to die; he charged Solomon). This recension marks the 2/3 division with the inline red ✣ cross rather than a coarse word-rubric 'ምዕራፍ'; the mid-chapter '✣ ክፍል ✣ <numeral>' blocks (seen on f029r-R after v.12 and f029v after v.34) are fine liturgical sub-dividers, NOT chapter heads — boundary was therefore anchored on the narrative as instructed. CHAPTER END: f029r-mid/right -> all three columns of f029v -> top of f030r left column. v.46 STARTS on f029v-R (line ~38, hence its 'column' metadata is f029v-R = where the verse begins) and physically SPILLS across the f029v-R -> f030r-L folio turn, ending mid-line near the top of f030r-L ('...ወቀተሎ ወጸንዓት መንግሥቱ ስ|ሰሉሞን በኢየሩሳሌም', with the word ስሰሉሞን split ስ on the last f029v-R line | ሰሉሞን on f030r-L line 2); 1 Kings 3:1 begins right after with 'ወተሐመይ ስሉሞን ሶፈርያን ንቱስ ግብጽ ✣ ...' (Solomon allies with Pharaoh) — OUT of scope and excluded; again only a ✣ marks the 2->3 division, no 'ምዕራፍ' word. METHOD: native JPEGs are ~1650x1700 px; each of the three pages was split into its three columns and every column upscaled 7x-12x with Pillow LANCZOS (multiple overlapping fine strips, plus targeted 10x-12x zooms on boundary lines and faded spans) to resolve the fidel; all crops were written to an OS temp dir outside the repo and deleted on completion. DIVERGENCE FROM THE PRINTED TEXT (transcribed as written, not harmonised): this is a genuinely distinct recension. In v.28 the BLACK running scripture is INTERRUPTED by 2 small-red 'እትርጓቚ' gloss lines (which are correctly EXCLUDED) and then RESUMES in black: after '...ወጐየ ኢዮአብ ውስተ ቤት እግዚአብሔር' the 2 red gloss lines ('ወእንዘ አቅርንተ ምሥሌ ዎቦ... / ግሥ ኢ ዮአብ ወረደ...') are skipped, then black scripture continues 'ሥዋዕ ወስእኩ ስሉሞን ✣ ሄብ ፈ ዮአብ እንዘ ይብል ። የዓናት እ ኮንከ እ ዘተመሣዓዐንከ በ የምሥዋዕ' (this restored black run had been wrongly dropped by the blind pass, which had instead carried a garbled tail 'የዓት አኩኒከሄ...'); the Barzillai-kindness clause in v.5b-6 runs 'ወአንተታ ወርድ ሲ በቱ በደየም ውስተ መቃብር ወሰደቴቅ ቤርዘሊ ገለዓዳዊ ግበር ምሕረተ'; spellings such as ሰሉሞን/ስሉሞን, ቤርሳቤሕ, ኢየሩሳሌም, ቄድርክ (Kidron) and the regnal numerals ፵ / ፯ / ፴ወ፫ are given exactly as inked. SYSTEMATIC SCRIBAL ለ/ስ: this scribe's rounded ለ was repeatedly mis-read as ስ in the blind pass; verified at >=30x (the scribe writes a DISTINCT narrow sawtooth ስ, e.g. v.8 ወተቀበስኒ, vs the rounded looped ለ, e.g. v.8 መዋዕለ) and corrected to ለ wherever the parchment glyph is the rounded ለ form: v.8 (መዋዕለ), v.23/27/32(x2)/33/44 (ሳዕለ). Tokens where ስ is genuine (ውስተ, እስመ, ምስለ, ብንያስ, አዶንያስ, እስራኤል, ወተቀበስኒ, ወታሴስል, እምሳዕሲየ, etc.) were left as-is — no harmonisation. FLAGS: genuinely abraded word-heads at column/folio turns (v.5,6,14,27,35); ቶ/ት sub-glyph borderline (v.4 ፍኖትየ); አ/እ sub-glyph borderline (v.5 እሜሳዶ); the restored divergent black v.28 run ('ሄብ', 'የዓናት' — recensional, read at >=30x); the faint black clause-end v.8 'ኤጣዕዱ'; and the faded penultimate line of f029v-R (v.45 'ሰዓለም', marked damaged). Text was traced physically continuously across every column turn and the f029r->f029v->f030r folio turns; the only black scripture the blind pass had dropped was the v.28 post-gloss run, now restored."
